# CODEFLOW Differentiation MVP

## Overview

CODEFLOW Phase 1 shipped an RTK-equivalent CLI (Bash compression + command dedup). This plan adds the 3 features RTK architecturally cannot copy: **File Read Dedup** (intercept Read/Grep/Glob via hooks), **Session Context Model** (track all tool calls per session), and **Waste Pattern Detection** (`codeflow stats --waste`).

These features shift CODEFLOW's token coverage from 25-35% (Bash only) to 80-95% (all tools), with target savings of ≥50% per session.

**Source:** [brainstorm-differentiation-report.md](./brainstorm-differentiation-report.md)

## Tech Stack (additions to Phase 1)

| Component | Technology | Rationale |
|-----------|-----------|-----------|
| Session log | SQLite WAL (existing DB) | New table in existing `codeflow.db` |
| File hash | blake3 (existing dep) | Already used for command dedup |
| Hook handlers | Rust (existing binary) | Extend existing `hook pre-tool-use` / `hook post-tool-use` |
| mtime check | `std::fs::metadata` | Zero new dependencies |

**Zero new dependencies added.** All features built on existing Rust crates.

